"To find the value of \\( b \\) when the point \\((a, b)\\) lies on the line given by the equation \\(3x + 2y = 12\\) and \\(a = 4\\), we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Substitute \\( a = 4 \\) into the equation \\( 3x + 2y = 12 \\).\n2. Solve for \\( b \\).\n\nLet's start with the substitution:\n\n\\[\n3(4) + 2b = 12\n\\]\n\nSimplify the equation:\n\n\\[\n12 + 2b = 12\n\\]\n\nNext, isolate the term with \\( b \\) by subtracting 12 from both sides:\n\n\\[\n2b = 12 - 12\n\\]\n\n\\[\n2b = 0\n\\]\n\nFinally, solve for \\( b \\) by dividing both sides by 2:\n\n\\[\nb = 0\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\( b \\) is \\(\\boxed{0} \\).\n\nFinal Answer: The final answer is \\( \\boxed{0} \\). I hope it is correct."
