"To solve the problem, we need to evaluate the expression \\(3 \\ast (6 \\ast 8)\\) using the given operation \\(P \\ast Q = \\frac{P + Q}{2}\\).\n\nFirst, let's evaluate the inner operation \\(6 \\ast 8\\):\n\n\\[\n6 \\ast 8 = \\frac{6 + 8}{2}\n\\]\n\nCalculate the sum inside the fraction:\n\n\\[\n6 + 8 = 14\n\\]\n\nNow, divide by 2:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{14}{2} = 7\n\\]\n\nSo, \\(6 \\ast 8 = 7\\).\n\nNext, we need to evaluate \\(3 \\ast 7\\):\n\n\\[\n3 \\ast 7 = \\frac{3 + 7}{2}\n\\]\n\nCalculate the sum inside the fraction:\n\n\\[\n3 + 7 = 10\n\\]\n\nNow, divide by 2:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{10}{2} = 5\n\\]\n\nTherefore, \\(3 \\ast (6 \\ast 8)\\) is \\(\\boxed{5}\\)."
