"To factor the expression \\(36 - 4x^2\\) completely, we recognize that it is a difference of squares. A difference of squares is a polynomial of the form \\(a^2 - b^2\\), which can be factored into \\((a - b)(a + b)\\).\n\nHere, \\(36\\) can be written as \\(6^2\\) and \\(4x^2\\) can be written as \\((2x)^2\\). Therefore, we can rewrite the expression as:\n\n\\[36 - 4x^2 = 6^2 - (2x)^2\\]\n\nUsing the difference of squares formula, \\(a^2 - b^2 = (a - b)(a + b)\\), we get:\n\n\\[6^2 - (2x)^2 = (6 - 2x)(6 + 2x)\\]\n\nThus, the completely factored form of \\(36 - 4x^2\\) is:\n\n\\[(6 - 2x)(6 + 2x)\\]\n\nSo, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\\boxed{(6 - 2x)(6 + 2x)}.\\]"
