"Let \\( t \\) be the number of hours since Jane started growing Sphere. Since she started growing Rod five hours earlier, Rod has been growing for \\( t - 5 \\) hours.\n\nThe population of Rod doubles every hour, so the population of Rod after \\( t - 5 \\) hours is:\n\\[ 2 \\cdot 2^{t-5} \\]\n\nThe population of Sphere quadruples every hour, so the population of Sphere after \\( t \\) hours is:\n\\[ 8 \\cdot 4^t \\]\n\nAt 8 p.m., the populations are equal:\n\\[ 2 \\cdot 2^{t-5} = 8 \\cdot 4^t \\]\n\nWe can simplify this equation by dividing both sides by 8:\n\\[ 2^{t-5} = 4^t \\]\n\nSince \\( 4^t = (2^t)^2 \\), we have:\n\\[ 2^{t-5} = 2^t \\]\n\nThis implies:\n\\[ t - 5 = t \\]\n\\[ -5 = t \\]\n\nTherefore, Jane started growing Sphere:\n\\[ \\boxed{5} \\] hours ago."
"First, we expand each product using the distributive property:\n\n\\[\n(2n-2)(n+3) = 2n(n+3) - 2(n+3) = 2n^2 + 6n - 2n - 6 = 2n^2 + 4n - 6\n\\]\n\n\\[\n(n+2)(n-6) = n(n-6) + 2(n-6) = n^2 - 6n + 2n - 12 = n^2 - 4n - 12\n\\]\n\nNext, we add the two expressions together:\n\n\\[\n(2n^2 + 4n - 6) + (n^2 - 4n - 12) = 2n^2 + 4n - 6 + n^2 - 4n - 12 = 3n^2 - 18\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the simplified expression is \\(\\boxed{3n^2 - 18}\\).\n\nFinal Answer: The final answer is \\(3n^2 - 18\\). I hope it is correct."
"We start with the system of equations:\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n2x - y &= 3, \\\\\nx + y &= 1.\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nFirst, we solve the system for \\(x\\) and \\(y\\). We can add the two equations to eliminate \\(y\\):\n\\[\n(2x - y) + (x + y) = 3 + 1 \\implies 3x = 4 \\implies x = \\frac{4}{3}.\n\\]\n\nNext, we substitute \\(x = \\frac{4}{3}\\) back into the second equation to find \\(y\\):\n\\[\n\\frac{4}{3} + y = 1 \\implies y = -\\frac{1}{3}.\n\\]\n\nNow, we need to compute \\(8x - 7y\\):\n\\[\n8x - 7y = 8 \\left( \\frac{4}{3} \\right) - 7 \\left( -\\frac{1}{3} \\right) = 8 - (-1) = 9.\n\\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{9}.\n\\]"
