"To find the area of an isosceles trapezoid, we can use the formula:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times (\\text{Base}_1 + \\text{Base}_2) \\times \\text{Height}\n\\]\n\nGiven:\n- Base 1 = 7 units\n- Base 2 = 17 units\n- Height (leg) = 13 units\n\nSubstitute these values into the formula:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times (7 + 17) \\times 13\n\\]\n\nFirst, calculate the sum of the bases:\n\n\\[\n7 + 17 = 24\n\\]\n\nNext, multiply this sum by the height:\n\n\\[\n24 \\times 13 = 312\n\\]\n\nFinally, multiply by \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\):\n\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{2} \\times 312 = 156\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the area of the isosceles trapezoid is \\(\\boxed{156}\\) square units."
