"When a right triangle is rotated about one of its legs, it forms a cone. The volume \\( V \\) of a cone is given by the formula:\n\n\\[ V = \\frac{1}{3} \\pi r^2 h \\]\n\nwhere \\( r \\) is the radius of the base and \\( h \\) is the height of the cone.\n\nIn this problem, the radius \\( r \\) of the base is the length of the leg \\( AB \\), which is 3 cm, and the height \\( h \\) of the cone is the length of the leg \\( CB \\), which is 4 cm.\n\nSubstituting these values into the volume formula, we get:\n\n\\[ V = \\frac{1}{3} \\pi (3)^2 (4) = \\frac{1}{3} \\pi (9) (4) = \\frac{1}{3} \\pi (36) = 12 \\pi \\]\n\nThe volume of the cone is \\( 12 \\pi \\) cubic centimeters. To express this to the nearest whole number, we get approximately 37.68.\n\nTherefore, the final answer is \\(\\boxed{37}\\)."
