"To find the radius of the circle in which a triangle is inscribed, we can use the formula for the inradius \\( r \\) of a triangle:\n\n\\[ r = \\frac{A}{s} \\]\n\nwhere \\( A \\) is the area of the triangle and \\( s \\) is the semi-perimeter of the triangle.\n\nFirst, we calculate the semi-perimeter \\( s \\):\n\n\\[ s = \\frac{8 + 15 + 17}{2} = 20 \\]\n\nNext, we use Heron's formula to find the area \\( A \\) of the triangle:\n\n\\[ A = \\sqrt{s(s-a)(s-b)(s-c)} = \\sqrt{20(20-8)(20-15)(20-17)} = \\sqrt{20 \\cdot 12 \\cdot 5 \\cdot 3} = \\sqrt{3600} = 60 \\]\n\nNow, we can find the inradius \\( r \\):\n\n\\[ r = \\frac{60}{20} = 3 \\]\n\nTherefore, the radius of the circle is \\(\\boxed{3}\\)."
