"To compute \\(\\tan 150^\\circ\\), we can use the fact that the tangent function is periodic with a period of \\(180^\\circ\\). This means that \\(\\tan(\\theta + 180^\\circ) = \\tan(\\theta)\\).\n\nFirst, we express \\(150^\\circ\\) in terms of an angle within the interval \\([0^\\circ, 180^\\circ)\\):\n\n\\[\n150^\\circ = 180^\\circ - 30^\\circ\n\\]\n\nUsing the periodicity of the tangent function, we have:\n\n\\[\n\\tan 150^\\circ = \\tan(180^\\circ - 30^\\circ) = \\tan 30^\\circ\n\\]\n\nWe know that \\(\\tan 30^\\circ = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\). Therefore:\n\n\\[\n\\tan 150^\\circ = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\n\\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}}\n\\]"
