"To determine whether the function \\( f(x) = 5^x - 5^{-x} \\) is even, odd, or neither, we need to test the symmetry of the function.\n\nA function \\( f(x) \\) is even if \\( f(-x) = f(x) \\) for all \\( x \\) in the domain of \\( f \\).\nA function \\( f(x) \\) is odd if \\( f(-x) = -f(x) \\) for all \\( x \\) in the domain of \\( f \\).\n\nLet's compute \\( f(-x) \\):\n\\[\nf(-x) = 5^{-x} - 5^x\n\\]\n\nNow, compare \\( f(-x) \\) with \\( f(x) \\):\n\\[\nf(x) = 5^x - 5^{-x}\n\\]\n\nClearly, \\( f(-x) = -f(x) \\):\n\\[\n5^{-x} - 5^x = -(5^x - 5^{-x})\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the function \\( f(x) = 5^x - 5^{-x} \\) is odd.\n\nFinal Answer: The final answer is \\boxed{\\text{odd}}."
