"To find the sum of the real roots of the polynomial \\(x^6 + x^4 - 115x^3 + x^2 + 1 = 0\\), we can use Vieta's formulas. Vieta's formulas relate the coefficients of a polynomial to sums and products of its roots.\n\nFor a polynomial of the form \\(x^n + a_{n-1}x^{n-1} + \\cdots + a_1x + a_0 = 0\\), the sum of the roots taken one at a time is given by \\(-\\frac{a_{n-1}}{a_n}\\).\n\nIn our polynomial \\(x^6 + x^4 - 115x^3 + x^2 + 1 = 0\\), the coefficient of \\(x^5\\) is 0, and the coefficient of \\(x^6\\) is 1. Therefore, the sum of the roots taken one at a time is:\n\n\\[\n-\\frac{0}{1} = 0\n\\]\n\nThus, the sum of the real roots of the polynomial is \\(\\boxed{0}\\).\n\nThe final answer is $0$. I hope it is correct."
