"To solve the equation \\(\\frac{3x+2}{x-1}=4\\), we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Cross-multiply to eliminate the fraction:\n   \\[\n   3x + 2 = 4(x - 1)\n   \\]\n\n2. Distribute the 4 on the right side:\n   \\[\n   3x + 2 = 4x - 4\n   \\]\n\n3. Move all terms involving \\(x\\) to one side and constant terms to the other side:\n   \\[\n   3x - 4x = -4 - 2\n   \\]\n\n4. Simplify both sides:\n   \\[\n   -x = -6\n   \\]\n\n5. Multiply both sides by -1 to solve for \\(x\\):\n   \\[\n   x = 6\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the solution to the equation is \\(\\boxed{6}\\).\n\nFinal Answer: The final answer is \\(6\\). I hope it is correct."
