"First, combine like terms on the left side of the equation:\n\n\\[2x + \\frac{1}{2}x + 2(1 + x) = 29\\]\n\nCombine the \\(x\\) terms:\n\n\\[2x + \\frac{1}{2}x + 2x + 2 = 29\\]\n\nAdd the \\(x\\) terms:\n\n\\[2x + \\frac{1}{2}x + 2x = \\frac{7}{2}x\\]\n\nSo the equation becomes:\n\n\\[\\frac{7}{2}x + 2 = 29\\]\n\nSubtract 2 from both sides to isolate the term with \\(x\\):\n\n\\[\\frac{7}{2}x = 29 - 2\\]\n\nSimplify the right side:\n\n\\[\\frac{7}{2}x = 27\\]\n\nTo solve for \\(x\\), multiply both sides by \\(\\frac{2}{7}\\):\n\n\\[x = 27 \\cdot \\frac{2}{7}\\]\n\nSimplify:\n\n\\[x = 6\\]\n\nSo the value of \\(x\\) is \\(\\boxed{6}\\)."
