"First, we need to establish the relationship between wands, rands, and fands. We know:\n\n- 4 wands are equivalent to 6 rands.\n- 24 rands are equivalent to 8 fands.\n\nWe can find the number of wands equivalent to 5 fands by using the relationship between wands and rands.\n\n1. Find the number of rands equivalent to 5 fands:\n   Since 24 rands are equivalent to 8 fands, the number of rands equivalent to 5 fands is:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{24}{8} \\times 5 = 30 \\text{ rands}\n   \\]\n\n2. Find the number of wands equivalent to 30 rands:\n   Since 4 wands are equivalent to 6 rands, the number of wands equivalent to 30 rands is:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{4}{6} \\times 30 = 20 \\text{ wands}\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, 5 fands are equivalent to \\boxed{20} wands."
