"To find the height \\( h \\) of \\(\\triangle PQR\\), we can use the formula for the area of a triangle, which is given by:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\text{base} \\times \\text{height}\n\\]\n\nGiven:\n- The area of \\(\\triangle PQR\\) is \\( 27 \\, \\text{cm}^2 \\).\n- The base of \\(\\triangle PQR\\) is \\( 6 \\, \\text{cm} \\).\n\nWe need to find the height \\( h \\). Plugging the given values into the area formula, we get:\n\n\\[\n27 = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 6 \\times h\n\\]\n\nSimplifying the right-hand side:\n\n\\[\n27 = 3 \\times h\n\\]\n\nTo solve for \\( h \\), we divide both sides of the equation by 3:\n\n\\[\nh = \\frac{27}{3}\n\\]\n\n\\[\nh = 9\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the height \\( h \\) of \\(\\triangle PQR\\) is \\(\\boxed{9}\\) cm."
