"To simplify \\(\\sqrt{192}\\), we can factor the number 192 into its prime factors.\n\nFirst, divide 192 by 2 (the smallest prime number):\n\\[ 192 \\div 2 = 96 \\]\n\nNext, divide 96 by 2:\n\\[ 96 \\div 2 = 48 \\]\n\nThen, divide 48 by 2:\n\\[ 48 \\div 2 = 24 \\]\n\nFinally, divide 24 by 2:\n\\[ 24 \\div 2 = 12 \\]\n\nNow, divide 12 by 2:\n\\[ 12 \\div 2 = 6 \\]\n\nSo, the prime factorization of 192 is:\n\\[ 192 = 2^5 \\times 3 \\]\n\nNow, we can simplify the square root:\n\\[ \\sqrt{192} = \\sqrt{2^5 \\times 3} = 2^3 \\sqrt{3} \\]\n\nThe answer is \\(\\boxed{8\\sqrt{3}}\\)."
