"To solve the expression \\(3^{-4} \\cdot 3^{-8} \\cdot 3^{14}\\), we can use the properties of exponents. Specifically, we will use the property that states that \\(a^m \\cdot a^n = a^{m+n}\\).\n\nFirst, let's combine the exponents:\n\\[\n3^{-4} \\cdot 3^{-8} = 3^{-4 + (-8)} = 3^{-12}\n\\]\n\nNext, we multiply this result by \\(3^{14}\\):\n\\[\n3^{-12} \\cdot 3^{14} = 3^{-12 + 14} = 3^{2}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the expression simplifies to:\n\\[\n3^2\n\\]\n\nFinally, we calculate \\(3^2\\):\n\\[\n3^2 = 9\n\\]\n\nSo, the value of \\(3^{-4} \\cdot 3^{-8} \\cdot 3^{14}\\) is \\(\\boxed{9}\\)."
