"Let $\\angle CBA = x.$ Then $\\angle DBC = 2x$ and $\\angle BDC = 90^\\circ - x.$\n\nSince $\\angle A = 90^\\circ,$ we have $\\angle ABD = 90^\\circ - \\angle DBC = 90^\\circ - 2x = 90^\\circ - x.$\n\nTherefore, $\\triangle ABD$ is a right triangle with $\\angle ABD = 90^\\circ.$\n\nUsing the Pythagorean theorem in $\\triangle ABD,$ we have:\n\n$$AB^2 = AD^2 + BD^2.$$\n\nSince $AB = 5$ and $BD = AC - AD = 1 - AD,$ we have:\n\n$$5^2 = AD^2 + (1 - AD)^2.$$\n\nSimplifying, we get:\n\n$$25 = AD^2 + 1 - 2AD + AD^2,$$\n\n$$25 = 1 - 2AD,$$\n\n$$2AD = 24,$$\n\n$$AD = 12.$$\n\nTherefore, $AD = \\boxed{12}.$"
